That depends on whether you have maxed out your Luck. I think that's a
reasonable assumption at this point, just as your 0% spell failure relies
on having taking the time to obtain non-metallic armour. Even with a +0
weapon, a 13th level character with maxed Luck has a +26 bonus to hit,
plus bonuses from Str or Dex over 16, which you may well have. You will
hit a monster with AC -6 or worse every time.

With a restricted weapon, you will hit a monster with AC -2 or worse every
time, even with no bonuses from Str, Dex, or your weapon. Few monsters a
13th level chararacter may encounter have a better AC - gargoyles are
about the only suspects here.

Luck has a truly absurd effect on to-hit chances.
